es:** 28\n2. **Red marbles:** Half of the marbles are red.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of red marbles} = \\frac{28}{2} = 14\n   \\]\n3. **Non-red marbles:** The remaining marbles are non-red.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of non-red marbles} = 28 - 14 = 14\n   \\]\n4. **White marbles:** Half of the non-red marbles are white.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of white marbles} = \\frac{14}{2} = 7\n   \\]\n5. **Blue marbles:** The rest of the non-red marbles are blue.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of blue marbles} = 14 - 7 = 7\n   \\]\n\nNow, Todd chose a white marble and kept it. This means that the number of white marbles is now reduced by 1.\n\n6. **Updated number of white marbles:** \n   \\[\n   \\text{Updated number of white marbles} = 7 - 1 = 6\n   \\]\n\n7. **Updated total number of marbles:** Since one marble (white) has been removed, the total number of marbles is now:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Updated total number of marbles} = 28 - 1 = 27\n   \\]\n\n8. **Probability that Hosea draws a white marble:** The probability is the number of white marbles divided by the total number of marbles.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Number of white marbles}}{\\text{Total number of marbles}} = \\frac{6}{27}\n   \\]\n\n9. **Simplify the fraction:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6}{27} = \\frac{2}{9}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that Hosea draws a white marble is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{2}{9}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{2}{9}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:57"}
